<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 26 February, from 747 BCE to 1993.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/babylon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babylon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">747 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,772 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nabonassar becomes king of Babylon, by Ptolemy's reckoning</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By Ptolemy's reckoning, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonassar">Nabonassar</a> became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. Ptolemy's list of kings, used by later astronomers, counted its years from his accession, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonian-chronicles">Babylonian Chronicle</a> also began with his reign.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabonassar">Nabonassar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius-ptolemy">Claudius Ptolemy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">364 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,662 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Valentinian I proclaimed Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers chose Valentinian, a Pannonian general, as emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a>. A month later he made his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> co-emperor in the East, while he ruled the West.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1074">1074 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">952 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Solomon of Hungary defeats his cousin Duke Géza at Kemej</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Kemej, in present-day Heves County, the royal army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> defeated his rebellious cousin Duke Géza, who had been betrayed but escaped. Géza defeated Solomon at Mogyoród that same year and became king.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geza-i-of-hungary">Géza I of Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1266">1266 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">760 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles of Anjou defeats and kills Manfred at Benevento</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles I of Anjou</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily">Manfred, King of Sicily</a>, who was killed in the battle. The victory gave Charles the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> power in southern Italy.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-benevento">Battle of Benevento</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles I of Anjou</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily">Manfred, King of Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1616">1616 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">410 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo is warned to abandon Copernican theory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cardinal Bellarmine instructed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a>, on the Pope's orders, not to hold or defend the view that the Earth moves around the Sun. His 1632 'Dialogue' led to his trial for breaching the order.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon escapes from Elba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With about a thousand men, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> slipped away from his island exile and sailed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He regained power without a shot, beginning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-days-reform">Hundred Days</a> that ended at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Grand Canyon becomes a US national park</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a> signed the act creating Grand Canyon National Park in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. The gorge, carved by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> River, is over 1.6 km deep in places.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1935">1935 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">91 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Watson-Watt's team demonstrates radar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Daventry, radio waves from a BBC transmitter bounced off an RAF bomber and were detected on a screen. The test led to the Chain Home network, vital in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-britain">Battle of Britain</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1993">1993 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truck bomb explodes beneath the World Trade Center</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamist militants detonated a bomb in the North Tower's underground car park, killing six people and injuring more than 1,000. The towers survived but were destroyed in the attacks of 2001.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 26 February <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-iv-of-bohemia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wenceslaus-iv-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wenceslaus IV of Bohemia</span><span class="tp">1361–1419</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/augustin-calmet"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/augustin-calmet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Augustin Calmet</span><span class="tp">1672–1757</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-hugo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-hugo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Hugo</span><span class="tp">1802–1885</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-bulgaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-i-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand I of Bulgaria</span><span class="tp">1861–1948</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aleksandras-stulginskis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aleksandras-stulginskis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aleksandras Stulginskis</span><span class="tp">1885–1969</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/talal-of-jordan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/talal-of-jordan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Talal of Jordan</span><span class="tp">1909–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-masherov"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pyotr-masherov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pyotr Masherov</span><span class="tp">1918–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/helen-clark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/helen-clark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Helen Clark</span><span class="tp">b. 1950</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 26 February <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roger-ii-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roger II of Sicily</span><span class="tp">1095–1154</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manfred-king-of-sicily"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manfred-king-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manfred, King of Sicily</span><span class="tp">1232–1266</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lorenzino-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lorenzino-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lorenzino de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1514–1548</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eric-xiv-of-sweden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eric-xiv-of-sweden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eric XIV of Sweden</span><span class="tp">1533–1577</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-ii-emanuel-elector-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maximilian-ii-emanuel-elector-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maximilian II Emanuel, Elector of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1662–1726</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-hippolyte-lafontaine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-hippolyte-lafontaine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis-Hippolyte LaFontaine</span><span class="tp">1807–1864</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carl-menger"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carl-menger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carl Menger</span><span class="tp">1840–1921</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/saito-makoto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/saito-makoto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Saitō Makoto</span><span class="tp">1858–1936</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-v-of-morocco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mohammed-v-of-morocco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mohammed V of Morocco</span><span class="tp">1909–1961</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
